- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The constructor suite names every seeded preset through `PresetIds` (.spec-md §3.3) while the ids still hold their step-15 text, so every fact keeps its meaning and its result. Every occurrence in the files below, comments included, switches. Afterwards `git grep -n -E "(src|det|pol)-[a-z0-9]" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests` lists only ids that are not seeded presets, and they stay: the test-local user sources of `SourceLibraryTests.fs` ("src-user-1", "src-a", "src-b", "src-c", "src-user-krf"), the tunable fixture "src-t" (`ExperimentRunTests.fs:79`), and the `SourceSpecId`s of `EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs:64` and `:106` and `SourceProjectionTests.fs:25`, which name spectral source specs (`SourceSpec.fs:243`), not Library presets. A fixture holds an id as an `ElementValueId` (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin'). (1) `ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs:46-48`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs:56-60` and `:76-79`, and `ExperimentProxyTests.fs:38-39`, `:197-219`, `:238`, `:338` and `:365`: each `BoundByEntryId (ElementValueId "…")` is `BoundByEntryId PresetIds.source600`, `BoundByEntryId PresetIds.polarizerLp` or `BoundByEntryId PresetIds.detectorIntensity`. (2) `LibraryProxyTests.fs`, `tryGetEntry hits a known id and misses an unknown id` (`:63-69`): it looks up `PresetIds.source600` and asserts `Assert.Equal(PresetIds.source600, s.id)`; the unknown id "no-such-id" stays. (3) `PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs`: `entry` (`:25-28`) and `bind` (`:67-68`) take an `ElementValueId`; `mirrorId`, `thinFilmId` and `plateId` (`:31-35`) hold the sample's `entryId`, and `sourceId` (`:37`) is `PresetIds.source600`. (4) `PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs`: the expected protected ids (`:140-143`) are the `.value` of the five detector and polarizer members plus the seeded sources' ids, sorted as today. `polarizer` (`:147-152`) and `extractedLabels` (`:173-177`) take an `ElementValueId` and compare ids, and their callers (`:153-158`, `:178-180`) pass the members. (5) `SceneProxyTests.fs:32` and `SceneRoundTripTests.fs:32`, `:38` and `:105`: `Some PresetIds.source600` and `Some PresetIds.polarizerLp`. (6) `SourceLibraryTests.fs`: `wavelengthOf` (`:38`) takes an `ElementValueId`, and its seven checks (`:39-45`) read `PresetIds.source600`, `heNe633`, `ndYag1064`, `mercuryI365`, `krf248`, `arf193` and `euv13p5`; the live-Library fact's detector (`:114`) is `PresetIds.detectorIntensity`, in its record and in the lookup.

**Acceptance.** After the switch, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with an unchanged count, every fact of ExperimentCollectionProxyTests, ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests, ExperimentProxyTests, LibraryProxyTests, PlacedSampleEmissionTests, PolarizerBehaviorTests, SceneProxyTests, SceneRoundTripTests and SourceLibraryTests holding its assertion; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.
